course: dictionary
lesson: 4847
title: A hygienist at work
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A hygienist is a trained health worker. Most often a dental hygienist cleans people's teeth. You may meet one at the dentist's. The word comes from hygiene, which means keeping clean to stay healthy.
explain: Read this sentence and look for clues: «Disclosing tablets colour plaque pink so you can see where you missed, and plaque left for days can harden into tartar, which only a dentist or hygienist can scrape off.» Plaque is a sticky film on teeth. Tartar is hard stuff that plaque turns into. Scraping it off is the job, so a hygienist is someone who cleans teeth.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence to check it. Put «a hygienist can scrape off tartar» in place of the hard word. It still makes sense, so your guess is probably right. A dictionary will confirm it.
fact: A hygienist is a health worker who keeps people clean and healthy.
fact: A dental hygienist cleans teeth, removes hard tartar and teaches people how to brush and floss.
fact: «Plaque» is the sticky film that forms on teeth; if it stays for days it can harden into tartar.
fact: «Tartar» means hard stuff on teeth that must be scraped off, usually by a dentist or hygienist.
fact: An occupational hygienist is less common: they check that workplaces are safe and clean.
exercise: «Disclosing tablets colour plaque pink so you can see where you missed.» What is plaque? | A dentist's chair | A kind of toothbrush | A pink sweet | *The sticky film on teeth
exercise: According to the sentence «...which only a dentist or hygienist can scrape off», who can scrape off tartar? | A baker or a builder | A teacher or a nurse | *A dentist or a hygienist
exercise: What does a dental hygienist do? | Bakes bread for the school | *Cleans teeth and shows how to brush and floss | Fixes cars in a garage | Sells tablets in a shop
test:  What does an occupational hygienist check? | *Whether workplaces are safe and clean | Whether teeth are white | Whether the buses are on time | Whether bread is fresh
test:  What is tartar? | A brush for teeth | *Hard stuff on teeth that is scraped off | A kind of tablet that makes teeth pink | A soft sweet
exam:  Which best describes a hygienist? | A shop assistant who sells sweets | A pupil who helps the teacher | A person who drives the school bus | *A health worker who cleans teeth and teaches good brushing
